{
  "title": "Ferry Pairs Under The Cap",
  "description": "## Task\n\nA ferry carries exactly two crates per trip and the pair is allowed only if their combined weight is at most `cap`. Given the crate weights in sorted order, count how many different pairs of positions `(i, j)` with `i < j` are allowed.\n\n## Input\n\n- `weights` — a list of integers sorted in non-decreasing order. It may be empty.\n- `cap` — the largest allowed combined weight.\n\n## Output\n\nAn integer: the number of position pairs `i < j` with `weights[i] + weights[j] <= cap`.\n\n## Example\n\n```python\nferry_pairs([1, 2, 3, 4], 5)  # returns 4\nferry_pairs([5, 5, 5], 9)  # returns 0\n```\n\n## Constraints\n\n- 0 ≤ length of `weights` ≤ 10^5\n- 1 ≤ each weight ≤ 10^9\n- 1 ≤ `cap` ≤ 2 * 10^9\n",
  "signature": "def ferry_pairs(weights: list[int], cap: int) -> int",
